# Line-ending policy for this repo.
#
# The team develops on macOS/Linux, where files use LF. This file makes LF the
# single source of truth in git AND in every working tree — including the lone
# WSL-on-Windows checkout — so line endings never surface as spurious diffs.
#
#   * text=auto  -> git auto-detects text vs binary; text is stored as LF.
#   eol=lf       -> text files are checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# Because this lives in the repo, it applies to everyone regardless of their
# personal core.autocrlf / core.eol git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt-and-suspenders: never convert known-binary types (no files like these are
# tracked today, but this keeps them safe if any are added later).
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.whl   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
